# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF regardless of the
# contributor's platform or local core.autocrlf setting. Without this,
# what lands in a commit depends on each contributor's git config --
# this repo was authored on Windows (autocrlf=true, which happened to
# normalise correctly) but that is a local setting, not a property of
# the repository, and a contributor with autocrlf=false would commit
# CRLF into the same files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary -- never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gguf binary
*.eval binary
